' =====================================================================
'  Anatomy of an invocation
'  EA-STD-TOOL-001 — Tool Specification Standard, section 3.2
'
'  The eleven steps of a single tool invocation, across the five
'  components of the reference architecture (section 3.1, figure 2.1).
'  Steps marked  ◆  are the ones where a defect in the descriptor
'  causes a failure that no downstream engineering can recover.
'
'  Viewing in VS Code
'    Install "PlantUML" (jebbs.plantuml), then Alt+D / Option+D to
'    preview. Local rendering needs Java and Graphviz:
'        brew install plantuml graphviz
'    Markdown Preview Enhanced also renders .puml blocks.
'
'  Exporting
'    plantuml -tsvg diagrams/anatomy-of-an-invocation.puml
'    plantuml -tpng -SdpiScale=2 diagrams/anatomy-of-an-invocation.puml
' =====================================================================

@startuml anatomy-of-an-invocation

title Anatomy of an invocation\nEA-STD-TOOL-001 §3.2

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam maxMessageSize 320
skinparam wrapWidth 320
skinparam roundCorner 4

skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor                #4A5058
  ArrowFontColor            #16181D
  LifeLineBorderColor       #B8BFC8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor   #F6F7F9
  ParticipantBorderColor    #1F4F8F
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF3FA
  ParticipantFontColor      #16181D
  ActorBorderColor          #1D6B45
  ActorBackgroundColor      #E9F5EE
  DatabaseBorderColor       #1F4F8F
  DatabaseBackgroundColor   #EEF3FA
  BoxBorderColor            #767D87
  BoxFontColor              #4A5058
  DividerBackgroundColor    #1F4F8F
  DividerBorderColor        #1F4F8F
  DividerFontColor          #FFFFFF
  GroupBackgroundColor      #FDF3E0
  GroupBorderColor          #8A5A00
  GroupHeaderFontColor      #8A5A00
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EEF3FA
  BorderColor     #1F4F8F
  FontColor       #16181D
  FontSize        11
}

box "Untrusted — input, never authority" #FFFDF7
  actor "Principal\ncustomer or adviser" as P
  participant "Agent runtime\nmodel · orchestrator · tool client" as A
end box

box "Firm control plane" #FBFCFE
  participant "Tool catalog" as C
  participant "Tool gateway" as G
end box

box "Domain" #FBFDFB
  participant "Tool implementation" as T
  database "Systems of record" as S
end box

participant "Identity plane" as ID
collections "Audit plane" as AUD

== 1 · Catalog resolves the audience ==

P -> A : "What do I own?"
activate A
A -> C : request the tool set for this principal
activate C
C -> ID : resolve entitlements
ID --> C : scopes held
C --> A : only the tools this principal may invoke
deactivate C
note over C
  Visibility is an entitlement decision (§10.4), not a
  convenience. Offering a tool the principal cannot use
  wastes context and discloses that the capability exists.
end note

== 2 ◆ Descriptors enter context ==

A -> A : render name, title, description and\ninput schema into the model's context
note right of A
  The standing token cost on every turn (§13.1).
  Target ≤ 25 tools and ≤ 10% of the context window.
end note

== 3 ◆ Model selects a tool ==

A -> A : choose **brokerage_positions_list**
note right of A
  The description must distinguish this tool from its
  nearest neighbor and say when **not** to use it (§6.2).
  Most misroutes are failures of discrimination, not
  comprehension.
end note

== 4 ◆ Model composes arguments ==

A -> A : {"accountId": "acct_01HQ8Z4M2X9K3P7R"}
note right of A
  The schema is tight enough that a plausible guess is a
  valid value, and enums prevent invented ones (§7.3).
end note

== 5 · Gateway validates ==

A -> G : invoke(tool, arguments, principal context)
activate G
G -> G : validate against inputSchema
alt arguments invalid
  G --> A : isError: true · INVALID_ARGUMENT\nremediation naming the offending field
  note right of G
    Structured and actionable, never a stack trace (§11.4).
    Every violation is enumerated, not just the first.
  end note
end

== 6 · Policy evaluates ==

G -> C : fetch descriptor + governance block
activate C
C --> G : riskTier · entitlements · approval mode ·\nrate limit · descriptor hash
deactivate C
G -> G : verify the pinned descriptor hash
note right of G
  A descriptor that changed without a version bump is
  refused, not tolerated (TS-SEC-09).
end note
G -> ID : authorize principal for the declared scopes
ID --> G : decision
alt not entitled
  G --> A : isError: true · ENTITLEMENT_DENIED\n"ask the customer to grant access; do not retry"
end

== 7 · Approval, if required ==

alt approval mode = confirm  (risk tier 3)
  G -> P : render confirmationTemplate with the **validated** arguments\n"Buy 100 AAPL · ••••4471 Roth IRA · est. 24,875.00 USD · cannot be undone"
  P --> G : approve or decline
  G -> G : bind the approval to a hash of the exact arguments shown
  note right of G
    Single use, expires in 120 s (TS-ANN-05, TS-ANN-06).
    An agent that could alter arguments after approval
    would make the approval meaningless.
  end note
else approval denied
  G --> A : isError: true · APPROVAL_DENIED · "stop; do not rephrase and retry"
end

== 8 · Implementation executes ==

G -> T : invoke, carrying the principal's delegated authority
activate T
T -> T : re-check entitlement for **this specific resource**
note right of T
  TS-SEC-08. The check that stops one customer reading
  another's account — and the one most often skipped
  because the gateway check feels sufficient.
end note
T -> S : read positions and marks
activate S
S --> T : rows
deactivate S
T -> T : apply domain rules\n(signed quantity, contract multiplier, totals)

== 9 ◆ Result is shaped ==

T -> T : shape to outputSchema · truncate to budget ·\nneutralize untrusted text · set asOf, basis, completeness
note right of T
  Truncation is disclosed, never silent (TS-OUT-07).
  Customer-supplied text — an account nickname — is
  delimited and labeled as data (TS-SEC-11).
end note
T --> G : content[] + structuredContent + isError
deactivate T

== 10 ◆ Model reads the result ==

G --> A : result envelope
deactivate G
A -> A : read both renderings — they must agree (§8.2)
A -> P : "3 positions as of 14:32 UTC. AAPL 250 sh long …\nTSLA 400 sh **SHORT** … prices delayed up to 15 minutes."
deactivate A
note over P, A
  Every domain convention the payload relies on was stated
  somewhere (§18.3). Otherwise this step produces fluent
  misinformation: nothing crashes, nothing is logged, and
  no test fails.
end note

== 11 · Audit is written ==

G -> AUD : traceId · conversationId · principal · agent ·\ntoolName · toolVersion · **descriptorHash** ·\narguments (PII masked) · outcome · resultDigest ·\napproval + argument hash · entitlements · latency
note right of AUD
  Retained to the tool's recordKeeping.retention (§16.1).
  Without the descriptor hash you cannot reconstruct what
  the model was told — the first question in any
  investigation.
end note

legend right
  | ◆ | A descriptor defect here cannot be recovered downstream |
  | §n | Section of EA-STD-TOOL-001 |
  | TS-xxx-nn | Normative rule identifier |
endlegend

@enduml
